A||||12||GodSend||Stereo install pics ||||1||
Z||000000||GodSend||06-25-2001||07:44 PM||||Looks like I am almost done, Just waiting for AusFieros consoles so I can install my IDQ 10'.... Here are a few pics, followed by a brief description<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/fpic1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/fpic2.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/fpic3.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/fpic4.jpg"> <P>The front stage is a DEI studio neodymium 3 way set.  I picked them up for a good deal from  <A HREF="http://www.nexxon.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nexxon.com</A>  which is an online stereo shop I highly recommend. The set consists of a 1" tweet, 5.25" driver, and a 8" midbass.  The dei midbass drivers havea  special set of magnets which are half on in the rear of the cone, and half in the front, so the mounting depth in minimum.<P>For amplifiers I picked two Rockford Fosgate RFG-2299's from  <A HREF="http://www.mmxpress.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mmxpress.com</A>  which is also a reliable online source.  They were on sale for 99$ bucks each, putting out 80*2 or 180*1 @ 4 ohms.  I have the front stage running off the left and right channels of one of the amps, and the other amp is sitting there ready to run bridged for a idq10'.<P>Sounds really nice so far, runs off a clarion head unit. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tweek||06-25-2001||08:58 PM||||very interesting...  though I wouldn't consider doing that because I drive the car in the wintertime and I wouldn't want somebody to ruin the speakers...   (I would be careful... but my wife is a little clumsy =))<P>Sound is good.<BR>Music is good.||||reg||1
